> Ordered centres make the synthetic source hand-checkable

For row i, component k=i modulo K has angle 2πk/K. Its two coordinates are
r(cosθ,sinθ)+σ ε_i, with explicit independent Gaussian coordinates. Setting K=4,
r=2 and σ=0 gives centres (2,0),(0,2),(-2,0),(0,-2), up to trigonometric rounding.
Components cycle deterministically; a remainder goes to the earliest components.
The native generator uses the existing seeded Double Gaussian stream, computes centres
and addition in Double, then performs one final Float32/64 cast. It does not shuffle,
choose components randomly or consume global RNG state. No downloaded data are needed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bigan_toy_ring.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
