> Three procedural pools and three small networks

Fitting uses 400 ring points with seed 5507; validation/test each 128 use 5519/5521.
Every pool cycles through eight components equally. Gaussian prior banks use 6043 for
validation and 6047 for test. The initial test forward is archived as a diagnostic control;
test outcomes never choose updates, epochs, hyperparameters or checkpoint weights.
The fixed schedule uses final epoch 3; no validation score selects an epoch.

| Store | Mapping and creation order | Leaves | Scalars |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| G, seed 6007 | prior2 → tanh16 → linear data2; hidden then output W,b |4|82|
| E, seed 6011 | data2 → tanh16 → linear code2; hidden then output W,b |4|82|
| D, seed 6029 | concat(data2,code2) → tanh16 → raw source1; hidden then output W,b |4|97|
| Total | Three independent parameter stores |12|261|

The canonical tanh/linear map implementation is reused for all three networks; no sigmoid
bounds the coordinates. The public forward also accepts positive unequal real/prior
pool sizes and inferred differing coordinate widths. The frozen experiment keeps both
widths at 2 and all computations Float32.

