> Held-out generation and encoding remain visibly weak

The blue points below are held-out data; red points are G applied to the fixed prior bank.
All 128 of each source are retained. G's output remains concentrated away from the eight
ring modes. Encoded points remain in tight groups rather than filling the displayed Gaussian
prior cloud. Every plot uses a square coordinate viewport, shared [-3,3]
limits, and reports points outside that window; all six plotted 128-point pools are inside.
A finite scatter picture is descriptive and does not establish distributional equality.

