> Both supplied pair parts matter to the restored joint discriminator

The restored D sees exactly the supplied data/code pair. Its score on(test,E(test))
matches the full real-branch score bit for bit. Replacing encoded code by zero changes a
score by as much as .2945093; replacing the image by zero changes it by .8831886.
The controls below plot all 128 original scores against their modified scores. The diagonal
marks unchanged prediction, not a target probability. D uses both pair parts, without a
hidden E/G call, a source label input or a new fit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bigan_pair_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/bigan/pair_controls.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  auto x = a.at("pair").to_vector<double>(), code = a.at("zero_code").to_vector<double>(),
       image = a.at("zero_image").to_vector<double>();
  double lo  = std::min(
             {*std::min_element(x.begin(), x.end()),
               *std::min_element(code.begin(), code.end()),
               *std::min_element(image.begin(), image.end())}),
         hi = std::max(
             {*std::max_element(x.begin(), x.end()),
              *std::max_element(code.begin(), code.end()),
              *std::max_element(image.begin(), image.end())});
  const double pad = .1 * (hi - lo);
  lo -= pad;
  hi += pad;
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.size(900, 950)
      .margins(90, 30, 90, 80)
      .points(x, code, "", {37, 99, 235, .7}, 3.)
      .points(x, image, "", {220, 38, 38, .7}, 3.)
      .lines({lo, hi}, {lo, hi}, "", {100, 116, 139}, 1.)
      .x_limits(lo, hi)
      .y_limits(lo, hi)
      .x_label("Original pair logit")
      .y_label("Modified pair logit")
      .title("Blue zero code; red zero image; grey unchanged diagonal")
      .save_svg("build/bigan_pair_controls.svg");
  std::print(
      "Max effects: code={:.9f}; image={:.9f}.\n",
      n::max(n::abs(n::cast(a.at("pair"), n::DType::Float64) - a.at("zero_code"))).item(),
      n::max(n::abs(n::cast(a.at("pair"), n::DType::Float64) - a.at("zero_image"))).item());
}
```
