> Reconstruction and latent cycle are unfitted diagnostics

The coordinate MSE widens before subtraction and averages both coordinates across all
128 observations. G(E(test)) gives 2.1331171; repeating the fitting-only mean point gives
2.0097662. Thus the learned composition is worse than the constant mean on this held-out
pool. E(G(prior)) gives 1.2355026 in code coordinates; this uses a different target space
and is kept separate. No residual chooses a checkpoint or enters an Adam step.

The idealized BiGAN result concerns matched joint distributions and optimal deterministic
maps ([Donahue et al., Theorem2](https://arxiv.org/html/1605.09782v7)); that premise is
unverified in this short run. An adversarial objective near2log2,
a low-dimensional code or the existence of E and G does not itself prove invertibility.
The reported residuals are direct finite-sample diagnostics, not likelihoods or ELBOs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bigan_reconstruction_mse.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a, data, noise;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/bigan/outputs.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/bigan/data.npz"))
    data.emplace(k, v);
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/bigan/fixed_noise.npz"))
    noise.emplace(k, v);
  auto mse = [](const auto& x, const auto& y) {
    return n::mean(n::square(n::cast(x, n::DType::Float64) - n::cast(y, n::DType::Float64))).item();
  };
  const auto mean =
      n::tile(n::mean(n::cast(data.at("fit"), n::DType::Float64), {0}, true), {128, 1});
  const double rec      = mse(a.at("reconstruction"), data.at("test")),
               baseline = mse(mean, data.at("test")),
               cycle    = mse(a.at("latent_cycle"), noise.at("test_z"));
  std::print(
      "| unfitted diagnostic | MSE |\n|---|---:|\n| G(E(test)) data | {:.12f} |\n| fitting mean "
      "data | {:.12f} |\n| E(G(prior)) code | {:.12f} |\n",
      rec,
      baseline,
      cycle);
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points({0, 1}, {rec, baseline}, "Data-coordinate MSE", {37, 99, 235}, 6.)
      .x_label("0 G(E(test));1 repeated fitting mean")
      .y_label("Mean squared data-coordinate error")
      .y_limits(0, 2.6)
      .title("Untrained reconstruction loses to the constant mean")
      .save_svg("build/bigan_reconstruction_mse.svg");
}
```
