> Prior-only generation responds to changed codes

The changed prior bank uses seed 6073. Its generated coordinates differ from the original
fixed bank, while standalone G(z) matches the full forward exactly. Standalone E(test)
and explicit joint-score calls also match their full-forward fields. Single/batch maximum
error is 0; restoring every one of the 261 parameters is exact, and all inference/control
calls leave the twelve stored tensors unchanged. Noise responsiveness alone does not
establish good coverage of the data modes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bigan_noise_control.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a, c;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/bigan/outputs.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/bigan/pair_controls.npz"))
    c.emplace(k, v);
  auto fixed = a.at("fake"), changed = c.at("changed_fake");
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.size(900, 950)
      .margins(90, 30, 90, 80)
      .points(
          n::select(fixed, 1, 0).to_vector<double>(),
          n::select(fixed, 1, 1).to_vector<double>(),
          "",
          {37, 99, 235, .7},
          3.)
      .points(
          n::select(changed, 1, 0).to_vector<double>(),
          n::select(changed, 1, 1).to_vector<double>(),
          "",
          {220, 38, 38, .7},
          3.)
      .x_limits(-3, 3)
      .y_limits(-3, 3)
      .x_label("Generated coordinate0")
      .y_label("Generated coordinate1")
      .title("Blue fixed prior; red changed prior;128 outputs each")
      .save_svg("build/bigan_noise_control.svg");
  std::print("Changed codes alter generation; inference performs zero parameter writes.\n");
}
